{"resultsPerPage":8,"startIndex":0,"totalResults":8,"format":"NVD_CVE","version":"2.0","timestamp":"2026-11-24T09:28:15.767","vulnerabilities":[{"cve":{"id":"CVE-2026-102664","sourceIdentifier":"security-advisories@github.com","published":"2026-11-04T21:17:41.300","lastModified":"2026-11-12T20:04:52.377","vulnStatus":"Awaiting Analysis","cveTags":[],"descriptions":[{"lang":"en","value":"ProxySQL is a proxy for MySQL and its forks, as well as PostgreSQL. Prior to 3.0.10, 3.1.10, and 4.0.10, decompress_mysql_payload() in lib/mysql_data_stream.cpp accepts a zlib stream when uncompress() returns Z_OK without checking that the actual output length equals the attacker-controlled payload_length. An authenticated MySQL client that negotiates compression can overstate payload_length, causing buffer2array() to parse the uninitialized tail of a heap buffer as MySQL packet headers and forward stale data to the backend. Backend error responses can disclose prior SQL queries, result data, credentials, or session state, and malformed lengths can also cause excessive allocations. This issue is fixed in versions 3.0.10, 3.1.10, and 4.0.10."}],"affected":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","affectedData":[{"vendor":"sysown","product":"proxysql","versions":[{"version":"< 3.0.10","status":"affected"},{"version":">= 3.1.0, < 3.1.10","status":"affected"},{"version":">= 4.0.0, < 4.0.10","status":"affected"}]}]}],"metrics":{"cvssMetricV31":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary","cvssData":{"version":"3.1","vectorString":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:L","baseScore":7.1,"baseSeverity":"HIGH","attackVector":"NETWORK","attackComplexity":"LOW","privilegesRequired":"LOW","userInteraction":"NONE","scope":"UNCHANGED","confidentialityImpact":"HIGH","integrityImpact":"NONE","availabilityImpact":"LOW"},"exploitabilityScore":2.8,"impactScore":4.2}],"ssvcV203":[{"source":"134c704f-9b21-4f2e-91b3-4a467353bcc0","ssvcData":{"timestamp":"2026-11-09T16:09:27.461578Z","id":"CVE-2026-102664","options":[{"exploitation":"none"},{"automatable":"no"},{"technicalImpact":"partial"}],"role":"CISA Coordinator","version":"2.0.3"}}]},"weaknesses":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary","description":[{"lang":"en","value":"CWE-908"}]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/sysown/proxysql/commit/396c742f7d50b1f479e1157e296ee9d0aff1b724","source":"security-advisories@github.com"},{"url":"https://github.com/sysown/proxysql/commit/a8c1cef4d44c4beea7f6aa21b8a09a7cb8c75520","source":"security-advisories@github.com"},{"url":"https://github.com/sysown/proxysql/releases/tag/v3.0.10","source":"security-advisories@github.com"},{"url":"https://github.com/sysown/proxysql/releases/tag/v3.1.10","source":"security-advisories@github.com"},{"url":"https://github.com/sysown/proxysql/releases/tag/v4.0.10","source":"security-advisories@github.com"},{"url":"https://github.com/sysown/proxysql/security/advisories/GHSA-fvch-fpgq-pwfx","source":"security-advisories@github.com"}]}},{"cve":{"id":"CVE-2026-84161","sourceIdentifier":"85b1779b-6ecd-4f52-bcc5-73eac4659dcf","published":"2026-11-06T11:17:17.190","lastModified":"2026-11-12T20:07:11.090","vulnStatus":"Deferred","cveTags":[],"descriptions":[{"lang":"en","value":"When an operator enables store.analysis_statistics_dir, a network client with PRODUCT_STORE permission for a product can call that product's storeAnalysisStatistics Thrift-over-HTTP method. CodeChecker 6.29.0 decodes the attacker-controlled Base64 string and passes the complete compressed input to one-shot zlib.decompress(). No maximum decompressed size is enforced.\n\n\n\nThis gives a correctly authorized, non-superuser store account a high-ratio memory and persistent-disk amplification primitive. The complete output is first materialized as a Python bytes object and is then written to the configured statistics directory. A sufficiently scaled payload can exhaust the API worker or host memory and impair CodeChecker availability.\n\n\n\nThe shipped value of store.analysis_statistics_dir is null, so the affected feature is disabled by default. The primary assessment does not rely on authentication being disabled. There is no authorization bypass and no path traversal in this report."}],"affected":[{"source":"85b1779b-6ecd-4f52-bcc5-73eac4659dcf","affectedData":[{"vendor":"Ericsson","product":"CodeChecker","defaultStatus":"unaffected","versions":[{"version":"0","lessThan":"6.29.3","versionType":"semver","status":"affected","changes":[{"at":"6.29.3","status":"unaffected"}]}]}]}],"metrics":{"cvssMetricV31":[{"source":"85b1779b-6ecd-4f52-bcc5-73eac4659dcf","type":"Secondary","cvssData":{"version":"3.1","vectorString":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:H/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","baseScore":4.9,"baseSeverity":"MEDIUM","attackVector":"NETWORK","attackComplexity":"LOW","privilegesRequired":"HIGH","userInteraction":"NONE","scope":"UNCHANGED","confidentialityImpact":"NONE","integrityImpact":"NONE","availabilityImpact":"HIGH"},"exploitabilityScore":1.2,"impactScore":3.6}],"ssvcV203":[{"source":"134c704f-9b21-4f2e-91b3-4a467353bcc0","ssvcData":{"timestamp":"2026-11-10T14:59:37.444938Z","id":"CVE-2026-84161","options":[{"exploitation":"poc"},{"automatable":"no"},{"technicalImpact":"partial"}],"role":"CISA Coordinator","version":"2.0.3"}}]},"weaknesses":[{"source":"85b1779b-6ecd-4f52-bcc5-73eac4659dcf","type":"Secondary","description":[{"lang":"en","value":"CWE-409"},{"lang":"en","value":"CWE-770"}]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/Ericsson/codechecker/security/advisories/GHSA-w57m-6g36-jjwv","source":"85b1779b-6ecd-4f52-bcc5-73eac4659dcf"},{"url":"https://github.com/Ericsson/codechecker/security/advisories/GHSA-w57m-6g36-jjwv","source":"134c704f-9b21-4f2e-91b3-4a467353bcc0"}]}},{"cve":{"id":"CVE-2026-125175","sourceIdentifier":"disclosure@vulncheck.com","published":"2026-11-09T19:16:52.527","lastModified":"2026-11-10T21:46:31.733","vulnStatus":"Undergoing Analysis","cveTags":[],"descriptions":[{"lan